cellPad: free the cursor while a menu is up (fps layout).

The fps layout captured the cursor whenever the window was in front, menus included, so in Resistance 3 the only way
out was Cmd+Tab: with the window in front the window's close button could not be reached, and a console game has no
quit item of its own. Now the cursor is captured only while the host's menu query (cellPad_set_menu_query) says no
menu is up: in the main and pause menus it is free (Esc pauses, then the close button or another app is a click away)
and the game takes it again when the menu closes. Mouse buttons and motion count only while captured, as before, so a
click in a menu does nothing in the game. Without a query nothing changes.

Test: libs/input/tests/test_pad_keyboard_fps.c test_menu_keys (released in a menu, captured again outside; fails
without the change). In play: the pause menu shows the cursor, resuming hides it.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

diff --git a/libs/input/cellPad.c b/libs/input/cellPad.c
index 3953fc26..f60049e2 100644
--- a/libs/input/cellPad.c
+++ b/libs/input/cellPad.c
@@ -528,3 +528,5 @@ static void pad_mouse_view(const PadMouseInput* m, double dt, PadHostState* hs)
  * title's; this follows the usual shooter one (R1 fires, L1 aims, L3 sprints,
- * R3 melees). The cursor is captured while the window is in the foreground. */
+ * R3 melees). The cursor is captured while the window is in the foreground and
+ * no menu is up (cellPad_set_menu_query): in a menu it is free to reach the
+ * window's close button or another app. */
 static u16 pad_keyboard_fps(PadHostState* hs)
@@ -556,5 +558,6 @@ static u16 pad_keyboard_fps(PadHostState* hs)
     static u16 ctx_held[sizeof ctx_keys / sizeof ctx_keys[0]];
+    const int in_menu = s_menu_query && s_menu_query();
     for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof ctx_keys / sizeof ctx_keys[0]; i++) {
         if (!pad_key_down(ctx_keys[i].vk)) ctx_held[i] = 0;
-        else if (!ctx_held[i]) ctx_held[i] = s_menu_query && s_menu_query() ? ctx_keys[i].menu_btn : CELL_PAD_CTRL_START;
+        else if (!ctx_held[i]) ctx_held[i] = in_menu ? ctx_keys[i].menu_btn : CELL_PAD_CTRL_START;
         btns |= ctx_held[i];
@@ -568,3 +571,3 @@ static u16 pad_keyboard_fps(PadHostState* hs)
     PadMouseInput m;
-    pad_mouse_poll(1, &m);
+    pad_mouse_poll(!in_menu, &m);
     const double now = pad_now_s();
diff --git a/libs/input/tests/test_pad_keyboard_fps.c b/libs/input/tests/test_pad_keyboard_fps.c
index 1f179d84..29a8a31e 100644
--- a/libs/input/tests/test_pad_keyboard_fps.c
+++ b/libs/input/tests/test_pad_keyboard_fps.c
@@ -155,4 +155,6 @@ static void test_menu_keys(void)
     assert(pad_keyboard_fps(&hs) == CELL_PAD_CTRL_CROSS);
+    assert(s_capture == 0);                              /* the cursor is free in a menu */
     s_menu = 0;                                          /* it started the game: still CROSS while held */
     assert(pad_keyboard_fps(&hs) == CELL_PAD_CTRL_CROSS);
+    assert(s_capture == 1);                              /* and captured again */
     s_keys[PADKEY_RETURN] = 0;
